I already reported this bug to the appropriate place, but I thought I'd
also post it here in case someone else runs into it.

I've had NetHack 3.1 crash twice so far on my Mac, a IIcx running
System 7.1.  The crashes happened while doing different things: once
while reading a spellbook and once when fighting a horde of soldiers
who were zapping various wands at me.  Both crashes happened in the
same piece of code.

If you have MacsBug installed, it will tell you that there was a bus
error at 'CODE 0053 08D2 timeout + 0C98'.  If MacsBug isn't running,
it will probably tell you the "application unexpectedly quit" with an
error code of 02.

If MacsBug is running, you CAN recover from this one.  Find the RTS at
the end of the 'timeout' routine.  It's at 'timeout+0EA4'.  Two
instructions before it there is a MOVEA.L instruction followed by an
UNLK.  Use 'G' to restart execution at the MOVEA.L, and NetHack comes
back to life.  It's probably smart to then save immediately and make a
backup of the save file in case it happens again.
